ared (family x model x tier) rows and only while the declared consent surface that turns managed selection on is present, drawn from a different model family wherever one is configured, degrading only to the documented same-family mode — with every selection logged before launch and a non-converging rework loop escalated through the declared approval level.\"\"\""," rationale = \"\"\"Realizes SN-026 (cross-family second opinions — every prior carrier of this contract demoted as routing machinery, so the sn_refs join forced the mint; SR-155 cites SN-026 too, for the planner pair, but only this row states the second opinion itself), SN-024 (an author cannot judge its own output) and SN-006. One row because routing, scheduling, scoring and escalation are one delivered contract — that the second opinion happens, independently, or its absence is documented — whose mechanics are the component details below it. The row also carries SN-026's DECLARATION and CONSENT half — `docs/agents.toml`'s pair-rows and the `docs/agents-enabled` surface whose presence turns managed selection on. That half had ZERO textual occurrence anywhere in the SR layer while `orphans=0` still held, because an orphan count proves a need has a citing row and never that the row carries the whole need. Managed selection is opt-in by consent rather than by configuration alone: a repository that declares families without dropping the surface has declared a capability, not turned one on, and the row now says so where a check can read it.\"\"\"","-acceptance_criteria = \"A declared review policy of N schedules N independent reviewer sessions; the declared (family x model x tier) pair-rows of the delivered agent registry are the only candidate source, and the declared consent surface's presence is what turns managed selection on — absent, managed selection is off and no row is resolved; present, exactly one row resolves per in-process phase and tier; a configured cross-family draw is preferred and its unavailability degrades to the documented mode, never a silent skip; every selection is logged before launch, never a silent model swap; rework iterates within the declared budget and pages per the declared approval level on exhaustion. The verdict that may clear integration comes from a session minted for that review over the whole lane, from its recorded claim to its reviewed tip; iteration rounds between full rounds review only rework since the last reviewed state, answer that round's findings, and never clear integration.\"","+acceptance_criteria = \"A declared review policy of N schedules N independent reviewer sessions; the declared (family x model x tier) pair-rows of the delivered agent registry are the only candidate source, and the declared consent surface's presence is what turns managed selection on — absent, managed selection is off and no row is resolved; present, exactly one row resolves per in-process phase and tier; a configured cross-family draw is preferred and its unavailability degrades to the documented mode, never a silent skip; every selection is logged before launch, never a silent model swap; rework iterates within the declared budget and pages per the declared approval level on exhaustion. The verdict that may clear integration comes from a session minted for that review, or, where reviewer retention is on and the declared final-reviewer setting selects persistence, from a round the coordinator recorded as final for the lane's retained final reviewer, over the whole lane, from its recorded claim to its reviewed tip; iteration rounds between full rounds review only rework since the last reviewed state, answer that round's findings, and never clear integration, whether their session was started fresh or resumed.\""," priority = \"S\""," verification = \"Test\""," status = \"Approved\""]},{"oldStart":739,"oldLines":7,"newStart":739,"newLines":7,"lines":[" hat_refs = [\"INTEGRITY-RECOVERABILITY\", \"UNATTENDED-OPS\"]"," requirement = \"\"\"The delivered loop content shall run ready work on bounded, mutually isolated lanes and narrow every lane back to the integration branch through one serial, fail-closed seam that runs the declared bar on the composed tree — parking a red candidate and stopping the queue loudly, draining claiming to a clean merged stop under a declared pause, and reconstructing claim and queue state from version-control history alone at any crash boundary, never a half-integrated authoritative state.\"\"\""," rationale = \"\"\"Realizes SN-027 WHOLE — ready work fans out across bounded parallel lanes and that fan-out narrows to one serialized gated seam before anything lands, in the need's own words — with SN-008 (the seam is fail-closed) and SN-025 (recovery from version-control history alone). ONE DECISION PER ROW: \"serial integration is one delivered contract\" is sound for the SEAM, but lane execution, claim authority and the trunk-side mint of work-item identity are not the seam, and a row stating the seam alone leaves SN-027's FIRST half — bounded lanes, isolated working trees, a worker ceiling — stated nowhere. This row therefore states the whole lane LIFECYCLE (claim, run isolated, close, land), which is what closes that hole; the trunk-only authority contract sheds to SR-170. The two fail independently: a perfectly serialized landing that lets a lane commit a regenerated artifact satisfies this row and not that one. Terminal close is SR-144's and is not restated here — one SR per (need, property), and both rows sit under SN-027 — so what this row carries of it is only that a terminal branch still lands through the one serial seam.\"\"\"","-acceptance_criteria = \"\"\"A launch with independent ready work runs up to the configured lane ceiling concurrently in isolated working trees, and a single-lane setting preserves the serial semantic; a finished branch reaches the integration branch only through the serial seam with the declared bar green on the composed tree — a red parks the candidate and stops the queue loudly; a declared pause stops claiming and drains in-flight lanes to a merged stop; a lane closed under the terminal-close contract (SR-144's, not restated here) reaches the integration branch through this same serial seam and by no other path; when a lane changes a claimed Done-when, its in-lane blessing binds the exact changed text before any subsequent build or rework dispatch, staged terminal close, or serial landing, while a review or adjudication session and the change's own commit remain unheld; a crash at any lifecycle boundary recovers from version-control history without double-assignment. A review-gated landing clears only from fresh independent review sessions over the lane from its recorded claim base to the reviewed tip; a partial-scope, retained-session, invalid, absent, or dissenting review holds the landing.\"\"\"","+acceptance_criteria = \"\"\"A launch with independent ready work runs up to the configured lane ceiling concurrently in isolated working trees, and a single-lane setting preserves the serial semantic; a finished branch reaches the integration branch only through the serial seam with the declared bar green on the composed tree — a red parks the candidate and stops the queue loudly; a declared pause stops claiming and drains in-flight lanes to a merged stop; a lane closed under the terminal-close contract (SR-144's, not restated here) reaches the integration branch through this same serial seam and by no other path; when a lane changes a claimed Done-when, its in-lane blessing binds the exact changed text before any subsequent build or rework dispatch, staged terminal close, or serial landing, while a review or adjudication session and the change's own commit remain unheld; a crash at any lifecycle boundary recovers from version-control history without double-assignment. A review-gated landing clears only from independent review sessions over the lane from its recorded claim base to the reviewed tip, each started fresh for that review or, where reviewer retention is on and the declared final-reviewer setting selects persistence, recorded by the coordinator as final for the lane's retained final reviewer; a partial-scope, iteration-round, invalid, absent, or dissenting review holds the landing, as does any other retained-session review.\"\"\""," priority = \"M\""," verification = \"Test\""," status = \"Approved\""]},{"oldStart":1871,"oldLines":3,"newStart":1871,"newLines":18,"lines":[" status = \"Approved\""," phase = 6"," form = \"cross-cutting\"","+","+[requirement.SR-239]","+title = \"Where the reviewer retention dial is on, loop review routes retain only their scoped reviewer sessions\"","+sn_refs = [\"SN-025\"]","+boundary_refs = [\"B-10\"]","+hat_refs = [\"PERFORMANCE\", \"UNATTENDED-OPS\", \"INTEGRITY-RECOVERABILITY\"]","+requirement = \"Where the declared reviewer retention dial is above zero, the delivered loop review content shall resume a reviewer only across iteration rounds for one lane, claim and review phase, keyed by those values and the iteration stage; read an absent, unreadable, malformed, misfiled or differently keyed retained record as no session and start fresh; never keep a reviewer session warm; retire that iteration session when the lane's full-lane round is drawn; run that round fresh, or, where the declared final-reviewer setting selects persistence, on one retained final reviewer per lane and phase that never resumes an iteration session; read a malformed reviewer setting, or a persisted final reviewer while reviewer retention is off, as retention off and a fresh final reviewer; and treat a change to the template a retained reviewer's brief is built from as a change of its governing inputs.\"","+rationale = \"A DERIVED requirement. The Performance, Unattended Operations and Integrity Recoverability lenses identify the operating cost, unattended judgement degradation, and shared-state corruption risk of repeatedly minting reviewer sessions. Repeated fresh reviewer rounds can exhaust the available plan, while scoped identity prevents one lane or review stage from inheriting another transcript. Lane decision D-001 (pending owner) records that the coordinator-written review-scope and session-generation records, not reviewer-authored text, establish final-review provenance; session-mode and keep-scope remain audit-only.\"","+acceptance_criteria = \"With the reviewer dial at zero, every review round launches fresh and merge-gate admission is unchanged. With it on, two iteration rounds of one lane and phase resume one session while another lane starts its own; a record under another keying, an undeclared record shape, or a record filed under another key reads as no session; drawing the lane's full-lane round retires its iteration session; with a fresh final reviewer the full-lane round is fresh, and with a persisted one it resumes only the final reviewer's own session. The coordinator's committed review-scope record is the gating record the gate reads: only a full-lane round it records as final, with persisted mode enabled, admits that resumed final reviewer; a retained full round and every iteration round hold. Each review session log records session-mode and keep-scope as audit-only columns.\"","+priority = \"S\"","+verification = \"Test\"","+status = \"Drafted\"","+phase = 6","+da_refs = [\"DA-017\"]","+aspect = \"unattended-loop\""]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-887\\docs\\archive\\last_approved\\README.md","C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-887\\docs\\archive\\last_approved\\acts.toml","C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-887\\docs\\archive\\last_approved\\docs\\requirements\\system-requirements.toml"]}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01HVGT8GmHJaZixA1GoySN2o","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
