{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfv4WPP8voGK3qKkBqE32","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Sitting 005 is recorded: the verdict is commit `8afbc6c01` and the re-attestation act is `1bb86a2fd` (act seq 107). Both carry `WI: WI-887`. SR-154 and SR-156 are re-anchored. Every other row stays unanchored, and no `Status` cell changed.\n\nThe rework answered all of 004's findings: LLR-140, LLR-207, TC-205 and TC-266 are fixed, TC-351 now claims only what its tests show, and SR-227 is back to its approved text. The new SR-239, which now carries the reviewer obligation, has its own problems.\n\n**Amendment: `VERDICT: MEANING rows=12`.**\n- **Re-anchored now:** SR-154 and SR-156. Only `system-requirements.toml` was copied, and SR-239 sits inside it still `Drafted`.\n- **Would bless, but stuck behind registry neighbours:** LLR-045, LLR-140, LLR-207, LLR-262 and TC-205.\n- **Withheld only because SR-239 is returned:** LLR-269, LLR-270, TC-266 and TC-322. Their own text is fine, but a child isn't approved before its parent.\n- **Withheld for its own text:** LLR-305. Its new REVIEW clause now answers SR-239, but its only parent is SR-227, which no longer covers reviewers.\n\n**First approval: `OUTCOME: RETURN rows=2`.**\n- **SR-239 goes back:**\n  - The rule that a malformed setting reads as off sits inside \"Where the reviewer retention dial is above zero\". Under that condition \"retention is off\" can never be true, so the rule never applies.\n  - Its acceptance criteria restate the gate-admission rule, which already lives in SR-156, and the audit columns. Neither is in the Requirement itself.\n  - It labels itself a derived requirement, but doesn't feed back to its need SN-025 the way SR-227 does.\n  - In sitting 004 I asked for decision D-001 to be cited in the Rationale. `trace.py` now warns that a decision-id citation is a history frame, so that advice was wrong. The verdict says so and asks for the reason to be kept as plain prose.\n- **TC-351 goes back for its chain only.** Its text is ready; re-sit it unchanged with SR-239.\n\n**Next sitting:** the drafts under each section's `## Dispositions` cover the rework: fix SR-239, add SR-239 to LLR-305's parents, and replace TC-322's \"ADJUDICATE identity is unchanged\" with the actual clauses. Then one sitting can judge and anchor the whole remaining set.\n\nThe `.requested` binding file is still untracked, left for the coordinator as before."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":465,"cache_read_input_tokens":310971,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":465},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d52360a6-7377-4d1e-a658-4cbc4052baa8","uuid":"d903c16f-6b57-495b-a6cf-18bcabb028c0","timestamp":"2026-10-11T07:33:02.669Z","request_id":"req_011Cfv4WP7Wwvw23VpRQx7WF"}
